  "prefLabel": "Env-Wr 101.17 Exempt dam",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wr 101.17 “Exempt dam” means a dam that meets either of the following:\n\n(a) A previously permitted dam that no longer meets the definition of a “dam” as defined in RSA 482:2, II; or\n\n(b) A non-permitted existing dam that does not meet the definition of a “dam” as defined in RSA 482:2, II.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Wr 100) #13979, eff 5-24-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wr100-900.html"
